[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656178357","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/2455#issuecomment-656178357","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/2455","id":656178357,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1NjE3ODM1Nw==","user":{"login":"benvanik","id":75337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-09T14:57:48Z","updated_at":"2020-07-09T14:57:48Z","body":"Oo this may be a much simpler repro than #2252 (which I spent some time digging through but was too complex to isolate). I'll take a look.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656178357/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656181078","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/2455#issuecomment-656181078","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/2455","id":656181078,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1NjE4MTA3OA==","user":{"login":"antiagainst","id":487928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/487928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst","html_url":"https://github.com/antiagainst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-09T15:02:18Z","updated_at":"2020-07-09T15:02:18Z","body":"Also attaching the vm IR for convenience: \r\n\r\n```mlir\r\n  vm.module @module {\r\n    vm.func @main(%arg0: !vm.ref<!hal.buffer>, %arg1: !vm.ref<!hal.buffer>) -> !vm.ref<!hal.buffer> {\r\n      vm.return %arg1 : !vm.ref<!hal.buffer>\r\n    }\r\n    vm.export @main as(\"main$raw\")\r\n    vm.func @main$sync(%arg0: !vm.ref<!hal.buffer_view>, %arg1: !vm.ref<!hal.buffer_view>) -> !vm.ref<!hal.buffer_view> attributes {iree.reflection = {f = \"I11!B3!d4B3!d4R6!B3!d4\", fv = \"1\"}} {\r\n      %c4 = vm.const.i32 4 : i32\r\n      %c50331680 = vm.const.i32 50331680 : i32\r\n      %ref = vm.call @hal.buffer_view.buffer(%arg1) : (!vm.ref<!hal.buffer_view>) -> !vm.ref<!hal.buffer>\r\n      %ref_0 = vm.call.variadic @hal.buffer_view.create(%ref, [%c4], %c50331680) : (!vm.ref<!hal.buffer>, i32..., i32) -> !vm.ref<!hal.buffer_view>\r\n      vm.return %ref_0 : !vm.ref<!hal.buffer_view>\r\n    }\r\n    vm.export @main$sync as(\"main\")\r\n    vm.import @hal.buffer_view.create(%buffer : !vm.ref<!hal.buffer>, %shape : i32..., %element_type : i32) -> !vm.ref<!hal.buffer_view> attributes {nosideeffects, sym_visibility = \"private\"}\r\n    vm.import @hal.buffer_view.buffer(%buffer_view : !vm.ref<!hal.buffer_view>) -> !vm.ref<!hal.buffer> attributes {nosideeffects, sym_visibility = \"private\"}\r\n  }\r\n```\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656181078/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656182615","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/2455#issuecomment-656182615","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/2455","id":656182615,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1NjE4MjYxNQ==","user":{"login":"antiagainst","id":487928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/487928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst","html_url":"https://github.com/antiagainst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-09T15:05:06Z","updated_at":"2020-07-09T15:05:47Z","body":"I tried to poke around. And here is what I found so far: we get an initial refcount = 1 for these inputs when parsing inputs and build variant list. Then we +1 to the refcount when entering the function in vm. And then when calling into `hal.buffer_view.buffer` the refcount for `%arg` was decreased by 1 in a non-trivial (in the sense of code layering) way: it's via `DispatchFunctor::ApplyFn`'s heavy templating. But `%arg0`'s refcount remains as 2 until the program exit and then it gets decreased to 1 by variant list free. So it still lingers on..","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656182615/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656185335","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/2455#issuecomment-656185335","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/2455","id":656185335,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1NjE4NTMzNQ==","user":{"login":"antiagainst","id":487928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/487928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst","html_url":"https://github.com/antiagainst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-09T15:09:57Z","updated_at":"2020-07-09T15:09:57Z","body":"I *feel* we might missing refcount clean up when leaving a vm function? But I'm not very efficient when parsing through the vm layers. ;) ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656185335/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656186126","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/2455#issuecomment-656186126","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/2455","id":656186126,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1NjE4NjEyNg==","user":{"login":"benvanik","id":75337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-09T15:11:22Z","updated_at":"2020-07-09T15:11:22Z","body":"I suspect it's staying alive in the stack somehow. For the buffer that is correctly freed the ApplyFn is doing a move (transferring ownership) and then release when the ApplyFn returns, hence the 2->1. I have some nice debug logging for the C++ ref_ptr type https://github.com/google/iree/blob/4e4f587b254c7e12aa3ceddb121a7cd54d4d1f83/iree/base/ref_ptr.h#L29 that I need to add in for the vm type.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656186126/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656195581","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/2455#issuecomment-656195581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/2455","id":656195581,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1NjE5NTU4MQ==","user":{"login":"antiagainst","id":487928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/487928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst","html_url":"https://github.com/antiagainst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-09T15:29:16Z","updated_at":"2020-07-09T15:29:16Z","body":"But should `ApplyFn` use move semantics? The `%arg1` view can potentially be used by another call following the existing `vm.call @hal.buffer_view.buffer`? I *feel* it should not change refcount at all and let the vm function exit to decrease? At the moment because `vm.call @hal.buffer_view.buffer` only takes in `%arg1` so `%arg0` is entirely left where with its original refcount = 2 after entering `@main$sync`. \r\n\r\n(But OTOH, I doubt we haven't hit the case that multiple uses of the same input view and don't know how that managed to not blow up thus far. ;-P)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656195581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656197022","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/2455#issuecomment-656197022","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/2455","id":656197022,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1NjE5NzAyMg==","user":{"login":"benvanik","id":75337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-09T15:32:06Z","updated_at":"2020-07-09T15:32:06Z","body":"whether to use a move or not is determined by the compiler:\r\nhttps://github.com/google/iree/blob/4c0a53e955c44480e2387a9d756a33f66830a394/iree/vm/module_abi_packing.h#L209-L214\r\nthe register allocator knows if a value is the last use and will add the MOVE bit - just like a C++ programmer would add std::move of a shared_ptr vs copying it and increasing the ref count.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656197022/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656199347","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/2455#issuecomment-656199347","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/2455","id":656199347,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1NjE5OTM0Nw==","user":{"login":"antiagainst","id":487928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/487928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst","html_url":"https://github.com/antiagainst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-09T15:36:47Z","updated_at":"2020-07-09T15:36:47Z","body":"Ooooh, of course, compilers to the rescue. :) :) :)  Very cool stuff! :D :D :D Eager to chat more. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656199347/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656276911","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/2455#issuecomment-656276911","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/2455","id":656276911,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY1NjI3NjkxMQ==","user":{"login":"benvanik","id":75337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/75337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik","html_url":"https://github.com/benvanik","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benvanik/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-09T18:15:25Z","updated_at":"2020-07-09T18:15:25Z","body":"I think I found the issue. For some reason I added a \"leak this ref\" line:\r\nhttps://github.com/google/iree/blob/b39149801a2c0dafaab23c06137db64962242745/iree/vm/module_abi_packing.h#L424\r\n\r\nThis would overwrite results from cross-module calls (like HAL calls) in cases where one or more registers were unused (or last-used) by the cross-module call. Will do a bit more verification and try #2252 as it should fix that too!","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/656276911/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]